a Colorado man accused of murdering his  family is expected to be formally  charged today police arrested 33 year  old Chris Watts last week on suspicion  of killing his pregnant wife and two  young daughters autopsies were completed  but officials have not revealed a cause  of death or motive  Omar Villafranca is outside the weld  County Courthouse in Greeley Colorado on  mark good morning  good morning Chris watts is in jail but  formal murder charges are expected to be  filed in court today now his wife  Shannon Watson was pregnant and she was  supposed to have a gender-reveal party  this past weekend but instead her family  is planning a funeral hey guys I'm here  with my little munchkins hi for those  who knew Shannon watts and her daughters  Bella and Celeste the unanswered  questions are almost as painful as the  grief the hardest part about it all is  when you're closer with the family it's  the why Chris Watts remains locked up in  protective custody accused of murdering  his pregnant wife and two young  daughters  the girls bodies were found on a  property where their father worked  submerged for days and storage tanks  filled with crude oil court documents  filed by watts attorney suggested girls  may have been strangled the defense  asked the judge to take a DNA swab of  the necks on the remains of the two  children the judge granted that motion  but denied a request for a defense  expert to collect their own DNA samples  from the hands and nails of the mother  and children he's the best thing that  has ever happened to me Shannon first  met her husband after a mutual friend  connected them on Facebook court  documents showed the couple recently  struggled with debt filing for  bankruptcy in 2015 over the weekend  Shannon's brother took to Facebook  writing I've never been so mad sad  enraged hurt heartbroken lost and  shocked in all my life the family's  friends and neighbors are also still  trying to come to grips with the tragedy  it's too close to home it's  heartbreaking that's heartbreaking  Watts is due in court again tomorrow the  big question in this case is why and we  could learn that why today if the judge  decides to unseal the affidavit Nora  everyone asking that same question no  more thank you
 

